# 316: an unknown escape reports the line the BACKSLASH is on (2), which for a
# multi-line literal is NOT the line the literal started on (1). Both numbers are
# defensible and the two engines share one lexer, so this pins which one the
# corpus asserts. The message shows the escape as written: `\q`.
--- source
let s = "one
two \q three";
print s;
--- expect
error: Lex at line 2: unknown escape \q
